      "description": "Vacancies | Work at the University of Amsterdam All vacancies Career fields Education & Research Assistant / Associate professor Lecturer PhD Postdoc Professor Researcher Research support staff Support staff Administration & Secretarial Finance & Control Facility Services HR ICT Management Marketing & Communication Project management Student & education support Student assistants & Internships Working at the UvA About the UvA as employer Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Career & Development Practical information for international employees Work at ACTA Work at Amsterdam UMC Log in I want to go to my candidate profile I'm an employee 0 NL EN Work at the UvA Vacancies Explore the possibilities at the UvA Please note: you will find even more vacancies on our Dutch site. View our Dutch vacancies Filter results Search vacancies Career field Assistant / Associate professor (6) Finance & Control (1) Lecturer (1) PhD position (14) Postdoc (4) Professor (1) Researcher (2) Student assistants &  internships (2) Faculty/Service Amsterdam Law School (1) Faculty of  Science (16) Faculty of Economics and Business (4) Faculty of Humanities (3) Faculty of Social and Behavioural Sciences (7) Experience Master's (16) PhD (12) University (2) higher vocational education/university (1) Possibility for hybrid work? No (17) Yes (14) How many hours do you want to work? to hours How much would you like to earn? $ 1 to 10 of 31 Junior Researcher (MA) with a Focus on Financial Colonial History and an Expertise in Art and Artist Faculty of Social and Behavioural Sciences €3,706 - €5,760 Closes on 20-09-2026 Master's Minimum 19 hours Are you an expert in financial colonial history and looking  to combine your (freelance) art practice with university research? We are looking for an researcher/artist (MA) for the research project “COLFIN: Colonial Durabilities in Financial Infrastructures,” directed by prof. Marieke de Goede. The project is funded by the European Research Council (ERC) through an Advanced Grant. For more information, see https://cordis.europa.eu/project/id/101199713 . View vacancy PhD candidate \"When vascular clearance fails: can brain networks be restored?\" Faculty of  Science €3,204 - €4,051 Closes on 15-10-2026 Master's 38 hours Are you looking for a neuroscience PhD project with clear clinical relevance? Do you want to study how brain networks become disrupted and how we might restore them? Are you excited to test novel interventions that target both vascular and neural circuits? Then this might be the chance to satisfy your curiosity. View vacancy Financial Administrator Amsterdam Law School €3,873 - €5,264 Closes on 28-09-2026 higher vocational education/university 16 hours Do you enjoy working in a fast-paced, international and academic environment? Do you have financial and administrative skills, and do you want to apply this in a non-profit and educational setting? Would you like to support our mission of advancing international and European law? Then join us as Financial Administrator at the Asser Institute in The Hague! View vacancy Student-Assistant for the Methods Desk Communication Science Faculty of Social and Behavioural Sciences €3,230 - €3,288 University Closes on 13-09-2026 Are you interested in research methods and in supporting student research projects through methodological advice? Since 2014, the Communication Science Department has a Methods Desk where students can ask statistical and methodological questions. We are looking for a dedicated and enthusiastic student to join the Methods Desk Team. View vacancy PhD Candidate in Flood Risk Modelling for the Financial Sector (Pillar 1) Faculty of Economics and Business €3,204 - €4,051 Closes on 17-09-2026 Master's 38 hours Are you interested in the impact of climate change and climate adaptation on flood risk and what this implies for insurers and other financial institutions? Are you motivated to bridge the gap between flood risk models and actuarial models that determine insurance premiums and capital requirements? View vacancy PhD candidate within a multi-methods project on negation across languages Faculty of Humanities €3,204 - €4,051 Closes on 12-10-2026 Master's 38 hours Do you enjoy working in an interdisciplinary research environment? Are you interested in applying multiple methods to advance research in linguistics and cognitive science? If you imagine yourself in a PhD position at the crossroads of lab-based experimental linguistics and linguistic fieldwork, then we welcome your application! View vacancy PhD Candidate in AI‑Driven Flood Scenarios and Insurability Maps (Pillar 3) Faculty of Economics and Business €3,204 - €4,051 Closes on 17-09-2026 Master's 38 hours Are you interested in AI applications in flood risk modelling, to answer questions that no existing dataset can address? Are you motivated by the challenge of generating credible extreme flood scenarios that lie beyond the range of historical observations and the current climate, so that we can describe the effects of climate change and the impact to the financial sector? View vacancy Postdoctoral Researcher in Damage Functions, Building Back Better and Early Warning (Pillar 4) Faculty of Economics and Business €3,706 - €5,760 Closes on 17-09-2026 PhD 38 hours Are you interested in the empirical foundations of flood damage modelling and keen to translate that knowledge into practical strategies for insurers to reduce losses through early warning and smarter recovery? Are you motivated to combine claims data, experiments and risk modelling to contribute to a more resilient built environment in the Netherlands? View vacancy PhD Candidate in the Macroeconomics of Flood Risk and Climate Adaptation (Pillar 2) Faculty of Economics and Business €3,204 - €4,051 Closes on 17-09-2026 Master's 38 hours Are you interested in the long‑term consequences of climate change and adaptation choices and the role that insurers and other financial institutions? Do you want to develop macroeconomic models that reveal where the tipping points lie in the relationship between changes in flood risk, financial markets and possible response strategies as protect, retreat and living with waterclimate adaption? View vacancy PhD position - Biochemical characterisation of signal integration in plants Faculty of  Science €3,204 - €4,051 Closes on 09-10-2026 Master's 38 hours Are you fascinated by how protein complexes allow plant cells to rapidly integrate environmental information? Do you have a passion for molecular biology, protein biochemistry and quantitative bio-imaging? Then this PhD position may be for you. We are looking for a dedicated PhD candidate to investigate the biochemical basis of rapid signal integration in plants. View vacancy 1 2 3 4 Show more vacancies Don't miss out on your dream job Set up a job alert and we will automatically notify you of new & relevant vacancies. Activate Job Alert Don't miss out on your dream job Set up a job alert and we will automatically notify you of new & relevant vacancies. Activate Job Alert Contact Privacy Cookies uva.nl This website uses cookies We, and third parties, use cookies on our website. We use cookies to ensure that our website functions properly, to store your preferences, to gain insight into visitor behavior, but also for marketing and social media purposes (showing personalized advertisements). By clicking 'Accept', you agree to the use of all cookies. In our Cookie Statement. you can read more about the cookies we use and save or change your preferences. By clicking 'Refuse' you only agree to the use of functional cookies. Functional Functional cookies ensure that this website can remember information that influences the behavior and design of the website, such as which vacancies are your favorites. Statistics Statistical cookies help us understand how visitors use this website by collecting and reporting data anonymously. Marketing Marketing cookies are used on this